        </p>

        <p>
            These Terms govern your use of PremiumMotors. By creating an account or using the
            site you agree to them and to the <a href="@privacyUrl">Privacy Policy</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">1. Operator</h2>
        <p>
            PremiumMotors is operated by <strong>Denis Robi</strong>.<br />
            Contact: <a href="mailto:drobi840@gmail.com">drobi840@gmail.com</a>
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">2. Acceptance and version</h2>
        <p>
            By creating or using a PremiumMotors account you agree to these Terms and the
            Privacy Policy. When you register we record the date and time of your acceptance
            and the version of these Terms you accepted. The current version is
            <strong>@version</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
            If the substance of these Terms changes we will publish a new version number and
            update the version recorded by the site at the same time. Where a change is
            material we will notify you and ask you to accept the new version.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">3. What PremiumMotors is</h2>
        <p>
            PremiumMotors is an online vehicle marketplace and <strong>introduction
            service</strong>. We do not sell the vehicles listed here. A vehicle sale is a
            transaction directly between the buyer and the seller.
        </p>
        <p>
            We are not a party to, agent of, broker for, guarantor of, or escrow provider for
            any vehicle sale. <strong>We do not hold purchase money, do not operate an escrow
            service, and do not process vehicle-sale payments.</strong>
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">4. Vehicle sales are between users</h2>
        <p>Buyers and sellers are responsible for completing their own transactions, including:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>inspection and testing;</li>
            <li>verification of identity, ownership, title and documents;</li>
            <li>mileage and vehicle-history checks;</li>
            <li>condition and defect checks;</li>
            <li>price and payment arrangements;</li>
            <li>transfer of ownership;</li>
            <li>taxes, registration, insurance and other official requirements;</li>
            <li>delivery or collection; and</li>
            <li>any warranty or statutory guarantee applicable to the sale.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            PremiumMotors does not guarantee a vehicle's condition, title, mileage, history,
            availability, legality, merchantability, fitness, value or suitability.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Nothing in these Terms removes consumer rights that cannot legally be excluded.</strong></p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">5. Private sellers and dealerships</h2>
        <p>
            You must accurately identify whether you are acting as a private seller or as a
            business. A dealership account comes with a public shopfront page.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>We do not verify dealership registration details, NIPT, VAT numbers or
            addresses against any register, and no account on this site carries a verified
            badge.</strong> Registering as a dealership does not mean anything has been checked.
        </p>
        <p>
            Where a dealer sells to a consumer, the dealer remains responsible for the
            statutory obligations that apply to trader-to-consumer sales.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">6. Eligibility and age</h2>
        <p>
            <strong>You must be at least 18 years old</strong> and have the legal capacity to
            enter into the agreements applicable to your use of the site. Do not register on
            behalf of another person without their authority.
        </p>
        <p>
            We do not verify age at registration. If we are told or otherwise learn that an
            account belongs to someone under 18, we will close it.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">7. Accounts</h2>
        <p>
            You are responsible for keeping your credentials confidential and for activity
            carried out through your account. Usernames and email addresses must be unique,
            and the information you give us must be accurate and kept current.
        </p>
        <p>
            You must not create or use accounts to evade a suspension, manipulate reviews,
            mislead others, commit fraud, or otherwise circumvent these Terms.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>Switching a personal account to a business account is one-way.</strong>
            There is no button to switch back; contact us if you ever need to.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">8. What may be listed</h2>
        <p>A seller must have the legal right and authority to offer the vehicle for sale. You must not:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>misrepresent ownership or authority to sell;</li>
            <li>falsify or materially misrepresent mileage, accident history, condition,
                service history, specifications, identity, location or title;</li>
            <li>list a vehicle you do not have the right to sell, or one subject to
                undisclosed finance, a lien or a claim;</li>
            <li>create duplicate listings for the same vehicle;</li>
            <li>list stolen, counterfeit or otherwise prohibited goods;</li>
            <li>use a listing to solicit unlawful activity; or</li>
            <li>upload content that violates another person's rights.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            Misrepresenting a vehicle's mileage is unlawful, not merely a breach of these Terms.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">9. User content</h2>
        <p>
            Listings, messages, offer notes, reviews, dealership text, display names and
            photographs are supplied by users. You must not submit content that:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>is unlawful, fraudulent, deceptive, defamatory, threatening, harassing,
                hateful or discriminatory;</li>
            <li>infringes copyright, trademark, privacy, publicity or other rights;</li>
            <li>contains malware or attempts to compromise the service;</li>
            <li>impersonates another person or organisation;</li>
            <li>exposes another person's personal information without lawful authority;</li>
            <li>is sexually explicit or exploits minors;</li>
            <li>manipulates ratings, reviews, view counts or marketplace functionality; or</li>
            <li>is spam or undisclosed advertising.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">10. Photographs and content rights</h2>
        <p>
            When you upload a photograph or other content you confirm that you own it or have
            the rights needed for us to host, reproduce, display, resize, crop, compress and
            technically process it in order to operate the service.
        </p>
        <p>
            You grant us a non-exclusive, worldwide, royalty-free licence for those purposes
            for as long as the content is retained by the service. <strong>You keep ownership
            of your content</strong> — this licence transfers nothing to us.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">11. Moderation</h2>
        <p>
            We do not review every listing before it is published, do not read every message,
            and do not currently operate an in-page reporting button. <strong>To report a
            listing, a message or a user, email
            <a href="mailto:drobi840@gmail.com">drobi840@gmail.com</a></strong> and we will
            look at it.
        </p>
        <p>
            Administrators can access operational data and may edit, archive or remove
            listings. We may act where we have reason to believe content or conduct breaches
            these Terms or the law, creates a security or fraud risk, or harms users.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">12. Suspension and termination</h2>
        <p>We may suspend, restrict or deactivate an account where reasonably necessary, including for:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>breach of these Terms;</li>
            <li>unlawful, fraudulent, abusive or deceptive behaviour;</li>
            <li>attempts to evade a suspension;</li>
            <li>security or account-compromise concerns;</li>
            <li>manipulation of listings, reviews, views, offers or advertising; or</li>
            <li>a legal requirement.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            Where we can, we will tell you why. If you disagree, reply to that message and we
            will review it. You may close your own account at any time — see section 19.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">13. Offers</h2>
        <p>
            Buyers submit private offers to sellers. <strong>Only the seller who received an
            offer can see its amount and content</strong> — other buyers never see it, and it
            is never public.
        </p>
        <p>
            A seller may accept or decline any offer and is never required to accept the
            highest one. A buyer may withdraw an offer at any time before the seller answers.
        </p>
        <p>
            When one offer is accepted, the site automatically declines the other outstanding
            offers on that listing.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">14. What an accepted offer means</h2>
        <p>
            <strong>Accepting an offer reserves the vehicle and releases contact details so
            the parties can deal with each other directly. The acceptance does not itself
            create or enforce a contract of sale.</strong> Any final sale agreement is entered
            into between the buyer and the seller, off this site.
        </p>
        <p>
            Neither party is bound by the acceptance alone. A seller whose sale falls through
            can put the vehicle back on the market.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">15. Contact details after acceptance</h2>
        <p>
            When a seller accepts an offer, <strong>the buyer and seller each receive the
            other's email address and telephone number.</strong> Use the other party's
            details only for lawful purposes connected with that transaction. Do not misuse,
            sell, spam, harass or unlawfully disclose them.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">16. Ratings and reviews</h2>
        <p>
            A review can be left only by the recorded buyer of a sold listing, once per sale,
            and not by the seller. Reviews are public and show the reviewer's username. The
            seller may publish one public reply.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>Reviews cannot be edited or deleted by their author after posting</strong>,
            and neither can a seller's reply.
        </p>
        <p>
            To ask for a review to be removed, email
            <a href="mailto:drobi840@gmail.com">drobi840@gmail.com</a> with the listing and
            the reason. We remove a review where it is unlawful, fraudulent, abusive, contains
            personal data or an allegation unrelated to the transaction, or otherwise breaches
            section 9. <strong>We do not remove a review for being unflattering, and we do not
            remove one at the seller's request because they disagree with it.</strong> We aim
            to answer within seven days.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">17. What is public</h2>
        <p>
            Information published on the site can be seen by anyone, including visitors who are
            not signed in, and may be indexed, cached, copied or scraped by third parties.
            This includes seller names and usernames, seller type, profile photographs, ratings
            and reviews, an optional public telephone number, dealership details, listings and
            their photographs, asking prices, price history, promotion status and
            recently-sold information. The <a href="@privacyUrl">Privacy Policy</a> sets this
            out in full.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">18. Public telephone number</h2>
        <p>
            A seller may optionally publish a public telephone number. If set, it appears on
            every listing that seller owns and is visible to signed-out visitors. Clearing the
            field removes it from the site, but we cannot undo copies already made by third
            parties or search engines.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">19. Sold prices are published</h2>
        <p>
            <strong>When a sale completes, we publish the agreed price</strong> on the Recently
            sold page, alongside the make, model and year. A listing's price-change history is
            also public.
        </p>
        <p>
            The seller is told this on the screen where they accept an offer, as well as here.
            The Recently sold page shows the last 14 days only; the end of that display period
            does not mean the underlying record has been deleted.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">20. Dealership pages</h2>
        <p>
            A dealership page is a public shopfront and may contain a business name, about
            text, images, city and country, address, telephone number, website and opening
            hours. The business supplies this information; we do not independently verify it.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">21. Fees</h2>
        <p>
            <strong>Listing a vehicle is free. We charge 0% commission on sales.</strong>
            There is no fee for listing, messaging or making an offer, and there is no
            checkout or payment processor on this site.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">22. Paid placement and advertising</h2>
        <p>
            Advertising is the only thing we intend to sell. There are two placements:
            <strong>Promoted</strong>, which gives a highlighted card and a position near the
            top of marketplace results, and <strong>Front page</strong>, which adds a slot on
            the front pages.
        </p>
        <p>
            Placements are time-limited and expire automatically. They never auto-renew. Every
            paid placement is labelled.
        </p>
        <p>
            Paying for placement affects <strong>position only</strong>. It does not change any
            fact about the vehicle, and it is not an endorsement, a check or a verification by
            us.
        </p>
        <p>
            <strong>No placements are currently on sale and there is no way to buy one on this
            site.</strong> Before any are offered we will publish the prices, the period, and
            the rules on refunds and removal.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">23. How listings are ordered</h2>
        <p>
            By default the marketplace shows newest listings first, and you can re-sort by
            price, mileage or age. Promoted listings are mixed into that order — two promoted
            listings to every free one, up to twelve promoted listings per page — and each one
            carries a <strong>Promoted</strong> badge. Promotion changes nothing except
            position, and a promoted listing stops being promoted the moment the car is
            reserved or sold.
        </p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">24. No verification</h2>
        <p>
            We do not inspect, authenticate, certify or verify any vehicle, seller or business.
            Do your own checks before committing to a transaction.
        </p>

